course: dictionary
lesson: 8106
title: Renewable energy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Something is renewable when nature replaces it, so it does not run out. «Wind, sunshine and flowing water keep coming back, so they are called renewable.» The wind keeps blowing and the Sun keeps shining, so we can keep using them.
explain: Coal, oil and gas are different. They take millions of years to form, and once they are used up they are gone. That is why they are called non-renewable.
explain: The word also works in other places. A library card or a contract can be renewable, which means you can renew it to make it last longer. Look at the words around it to decide which meaning fits.
fact: Renewable means nature can replace it, so it will not run out.
fact: Renewable energy sources include sunlight (solar), wind, moving water (hydro), tides, waves, heat from inside the Earth (geothermal) and wood and plants (biomass).
fact: «Renewable resources, such as sunlight, wind and flowing water, are not used up.»
fact: Coal, oil and gas are non-renewable: they take millions of years to form and will run out.
fact: Burning coal or gas adds to climate change, but renewable energy makes far less carbon dioxide. Saving energy helps too: lights off, LED bulbs on.
exercise: Which one is a renewable energy source? | *Wind | Coal | Gas | Oil
exercise: A library card can be renewable. What does that mean? | It is made of wood | It will be used up after one day | *It can be renewed to last longer | It can only be used in winter
exercise: Which word is the opposite of renewable? | Solar | *Non-renewable | Tidal | Geothermal
test: «Renewable resources, such as sunlight, wind and flowing water, are not used up.» What does "not used up" mean? | They run out quickly | They are made in factories | *They are replaced by nature and do not run out | They are only useful at night
test: Why is burning coal worse for the planet than using wind? | *It adds to climate change by making carbon dioxide | It is cheaper | It makes the Sun shine less | It makes the wind stop
exam: A contract is renewable. What does that most likely mean? | It is made from wood | It is a kind of sunlight | *It can be renewed to last longer | It must be thrown away today
